<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The app's user-facing strings: the single source for Android, iOS and the
    shared module. moko-resources generates MR.strings, the Android string
    resources and the iOS Localizable.strings from this file. Translations go
    in a sibling <languageCode>/strings.xml (see README "Localization").

    Escape like an Android resource (\' \" &amp;). Format arguments are
    positional (%1$s, %2$d) so translations can reorder them; copy that
    changes with a count belongs in plurals.xml.

    Keys ending in _ios hold copy that differs from the Android wording of
    the same element today (e.g. "Add to cart" vs "Add to Cart"); unifying a
    pair is a deliberate visual change that needs the screenshot baselines
    re-recorded on both platforms.
-->
